-------------+-------+-----------
           3 | 3     | 3

--- B. THE FINDING. queue_lanes is a GLOBAL in-flight ceiling, not a per-worker one:
---    v_room = least(p_limit, queue_lanes) - in_flight. alpha passed no limit (which is
---    what core/axs_watch_reader.run_queue does, batch=None), so it took all 3 lanes and
---    beta STARVES. A second worker needs queue_lanes raised to have room to work in.
 beta_items |     reason     | hold_s | in_flight 
------------+----------------+--------+-----------
          0 | all lanes busy | 2      | 3

--- B2. raise the lanes and beta gets work at once, on DIFFERENT events (rule 1)
